==Latin==

===Etymology===
From a shortening of ''II S'' where ''II'' is 2 in {{w|Roman numerals}} and ''S'' stands for {{m|la|sēmis||half}}. This is because a [[sesterce]] was worth 2 and a half [[as|asses]].

===Symbol===
{{head|la|symbol}}

# {{non-gloss definition|The symbol used to precede a number to indicate that the number is a value in [[sesterce]]s.}}

